# Block decode cost on a CPU: per-tone, full window ladder and table ladder

Generated by `decode_bench.cpp` with 13 threads. One decode scores all 2^k messages of one hypothesis.
Every measurement keeps all threads busy with tasks of one (repetition, high half) and does at least
6e+10 lookups; small blocks are repeated, large ones are timed on a sample of high halves and scaled
(`timed` gives the number of decodes actually done). Synthetic 4-bit tables with a planted message.

## k = 10 bits (1024 messages)

Per-tone (energy) decode: 1.054e-06 s per decode, 9.49e+05 decodes/s, 3.11e+10 lookups/s; timed 1.831e+06 decodes; planted message found.

Per-tone decode by fast Walsh-Hadamard transform: 2.324e-06 s per decode, 4.304e+05 decodes/s; timed 195312 decodes; planted message found.

| tones in the block | ladder rungs | s per decode | decodes/s | message-tones/s | timed decodes | planted on the whole-block rung |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 128 | 7 | 7.882e-06 | 1.269e+05 | 1.66e+10 | 4.578e+05 | yes |
| 512 | 9 | 3.433e-05 | 2.913e+04 | 1.53e+10 | 1.144e+05 | yes |
| 2048 | 11 | 0.0001396 | 7165 | 1.5e+10 | 2.861e+04 | yes |
| 8192 | 13 | 0.0005267 | 1899 | 1.59e+10 | 7153 | yes |
| 32768 | 15 | 0.002163 | 462.3 | 1.55e+10 | 1789 | yes |

| windows W (table ladder) | rungs | s per decode | decodes/s | lookups/s | timed decodes | planted on the whole-block rung |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 16 | 5 | 2.55e-05 | 3.922e+04 | 2.06e+10 | 1.144e+05 | yes |
| 64 | 7 | 0.0001295 | 7722 | 1.62e+10 | 2.861e+04 | yes |
| 256 | 9 | 0.0004905 | 2039 | 1.71e+10 | 7153 | yes |

